shape theory.discreteness : theory.transformation {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 3.5 (Moment Discreteness).
// The moment sequence is inherently discrete. Each moment M' is
// produced by exactly one application of the transformation law.
// There is no fractional application.
//
// The transformation takes complete input (C, S) and produces
// complete output (M'). Any proposed intermediate state would itself
// be a moment, introducing additional steps, not subdividing the step.
//
// Every shape has a structural minimum: the simplest coherent
// configuration. Below this minimum, the structure cannot sustain
// coherent transformation. The moment sequence has a structural floor.
//
// Note: discreteness of the moment sequence does not imply discreteness
// of character values. Character can take values in a continuous space.
// The continuous limit is well-defined but unreachable.
//
// Derives from: theory.transformation
  """
}
